// The Go workspace that joins this repository's modules (ADR-0059 decision 9).
//
// Three modules live here, and the split is not bookkeeping:
//
//   - `.`            the server. It has the whole dependency graph.
//   - `./pluginapi`  the contract. No requires, ever — a plugin author imports
//                    the wire types without importing the server.
//   - `./pluginsdk`  the Go SDK for plugin authors. Requires pluginapi and
//                    nothing else.
//
// The workspace is what makes `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...`
// from the repository root cover all three at once while each still resolves its
// own imports the way a consumer outside this repository would. The server's
// go.mod carries a `replace` for the two local modules as well, so a build with
// GOWORK=off — which is what a plugin's own `GOOS=wasip1` build runs under — still
// resolves them from the working tree rather than from a proxy that has never
// heard of them.
//
// Each `./plugins/<id>` is a Bundled plugin: its own module, requiring the SDK
// and nothing else, built to WebAssembly by `make plugins` and embedded by
// internal/bundled. They are listed here so that `go build`, `go vet` and
// `go test` over the explicit patterns in the Makefile's GOPKGS cover them — and
// so that a plugin's own guest build resolves pluginapi and pluginsdk from this
// working tree rather than from a proxy that has never heard of them. Each new
// plugin adds ONE line below (.scratch/bundled-plugins: issues 05-07).
go 1.26.5

use (
	.
	./pluginapi
	./pluginsdk
	./plugins/tmdb
	./plugins/omdb
	./plugins/thetvdb
	./plugins/anidb
	./plugins/musicbrainz
	./plugins/fanarttv
	./plugins/theaudiodb
	./plugins/opensubtitles
)
